# Every pattern that names a top-level directory is anchored with a leading
# slash, and that is not cosmetic.
#
# An unanchored `data/` matches a directory called `data` at *any* depth, so
# it silently swallowed `src/data/` — and `src/data/task.py`, which holds
# the block randomisation, the place target and `check_success`, was never
# committed. A fresh clone of this repository could not import `src.data`,
# so it could not run anything, for as long as the pattern existed. CI would
# have caught it on the first push; CI had been disabled since August.
#
# Keep the anchors. The patterns that are meant to match anywhere — caches,
# editor directories — are deliberately left unanchored below.

# Virtual environment
/.venv/

# Third-party assets
/mujoco_menagerie/
/graphify-out/

# Data and outputs — large, regenerable
/data/
/outputs/
/logs/
/wandb/

# Generated scene (rebuild with build_scene.py)
/models/

# Python — these may appear at any depth
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/

# Local agent tooling
/.claude/

# Editor — may appear at any depth
.vscode/
.idea/
